  "name": "Question 9",
  "problem": "John bought a bouquet of $4$ roses for $$5.$ What is the price per rose?",
  "worked_solution": "The ratio of dollars to roses is $5:4.$ Expressing this as a fraction, we have:\n\n$$\n\\frac{5}{4}\n$$\n\nWe can convert this fraction to a decimal by multiplying the numerator and denominator by $25:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{5\\times 25}{4\\times 25}=\\frac{125}{100}=1.25\n$$\n\nConsequently, the cost is $$1.25$ per rose.",
